# training-atr-models — asteraix (130.92.59.242)
#
# Copy to .env. The unit reads it with EnvironmentFile=.
#
# IMPORTANT, and new since the split: until 16.09.2026 the gateway and the
# trainer read the SAME .env on one machine. They now read two files on two
# machines, and four values have to agree across them or the handover breaks
# silently. They are marked >>> SHARED <<< below.

# ── the shared secret ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# >>> SHARED <<< with idhefix. Used in both directions now: idhefix presents it
# to this host's /train/* proxy target, and this host presents it to idhefix for
# the promotion gate and for eval/.
ATR_API_KEY=replace-with-a-long-random-shared-secret

# ── where the corpora and the trained weights live ───────────────────────────
# The research share, mounted on BOTH machines. That is what makes the handover
# cheap: the gateway on idhefix reads a path this host wrote, and the 48 job
# records written before the split are already readable here.
ATR_TRAIN_JOBS_ROOT=/mnt/wbkolleg_dh_1/Textrecognition_Training/training_folder/jobs
# >>> SHARED <<< with idhefix — the gateway resolves ModelSpec.local_path against
# this. A mismatch does not report a missing file: kraken_loader.resolve_weights
# returns None for a path that does not exist, and None means "fetch by DOI".
ATR_TRAIN_TRAINED_ROOT=/mnt/wbkolleg_dh_1/Textrecognition_Training/training_folder/trained

# ── what must NOT go on the share ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both of these are local *because the share broke them*, not as an optimisation:
#   checkpoints — the trainer saves via temp-file + rename, which is cross-device
#                 on CIFS (training/settings.py:43-50)
#   TMPDIR      — the datasets Arrow cache on the share cost one run 11½ hours
#                 (training/preflight.py:151-175)
# ATR_TRAIN_CHECKPOINT_ROOT defaults to ~/atr-cache/checkpoints; leave it local.
TMPDIR=/home/tobias/atr-cache/tmp

# ── the artefact cache (#109) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local disk, 100 GB budget. Note that it does NOT follow the data: the same
# share gives this host the same ground truth and the same HF cache, but a COLD
# artefact cache — the compile per selection is paid once more here.
# ATR_TRAIN_ARTEFACT_CACHE_ROOT=/home/tobias/atr-cache/artefacts

# ── the model registry ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# >>> SHARED <<< — the gateway on idhefix PUBLISHES this file here
# (serving-atr-inference#138); this host only reads it, and only kraken ever
# does, to resolve a base_model given as a registry id. It is on the share and
# not in this repo on purpose: a copy here would drift without a word.
# The default in settings.py is already this path; it is repeated here because
# it is one of the values that must agree across the two machines.
ATR_TRAIN_MODELS_CONFIG=/mnt/wbkolleg_dh_1/Textrecognition_Training/registry/models.yaml

# ── the gateway on idhefix ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two of the three HTTP edges across the seam point here: the promotion gate
# (training/promote.py) and, after the move, eval/. No longer loopback.
ATR_TRAIN_GATEWAY_URL=http://130.92.59.240:8200
# >>> SHARED <<< — the same key as ATR_API_KEY above.
ATR_TRAIN_GATEWAY_API_KEY=replace-with-a-long-random-shared-secret

# ── the HF hub cache ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT set here, and that is deliberate: ~/.cache/huggingface/hub is a symlink to
# /mnt/wbkolleg_dh_1/Textrecognition_Training/hf_hub (set 16.09.2026, write test
# passed), shared with the separate lassberg/vlm_training project. Setting
# HF_HOME would route around the symlink and re-download 6.6 TB.
#
# Open question, recorded rather than answered: two *projects* already write that
# cache; two *hosts* is untested. The documented CIFS issue is dedup, explicitly
# "harmless but not optimal" — not concurrency.
# HF_HOME=   <- leave unset

# ── bind ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Until the split this bound 127.0.0.1 and that WAS the whole security model —
# the service has no authentication of its own. Opening it to idhefix without
# adding a key first is the one change that must not happen alone (#13).
ATR_TRAIN_HOST=127.0.0.1
ATR_TRAIN_PORT=8204
